{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1493730-wyrm-cults","id":1493730,"title":"Wyrm cults","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-26T08:43:50-07:00","id":1493730,"title":"Wyrm cults","content":"How to simulate human Wyrm cults without using other splats? I\u2019d like a cult led by a \u2018magus\u2019, but he\u2019s not a mage, Sorcerer, shapeshifter or Kinfolk. How to do this? Maybe give him some special \u2018mark\u2019, visible or invisible, that allows him to learn Rank One Wyrm Gifts and Rank One Wyrm Rites? Make him a particularly clever fomor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T09:45:21-07:00","id":1493738,"title":"","content":"Well a Black Spiral Dancer Kinfolk could be a good start but you can also choose a mere humans intoxicated by the wyrm corruption through chemical or his deep faith into the wyrm impusle. You can use for that the different aspect of the wyrm like the eater of soul, beast of war, defiler or another, the wyrm is described as an hydra so you can choose any corruption you want and describe the character as so sensitive of the aspect you choosed that he slowly turn into something else. <br /> <br /> After that under the wyrm influence he will start to propagate the corruption through drugs, violence or anything and people that are sensitive to it would try to join him to get more.<br /> <br /> You can then include banes and use their power to posess some or manifest themselves as proof of the cult powers.<br /> <br /> I can suggest you to put your hand on the wyrm book, it contains a lot of detail about the wyrm, his minions and his powers, that would surely help you get what you need","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T09:52:32-07:00","id":1493740,"title":"","content":"Just give them access to whatever Gifts and Rites (and even Fetishes) which seem appropriate, with any that require Rage, Gnosis, etc. using Willpower instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T10:59:46-07:00","id":1493746,"title":"","content":"The thing is, the \u201cmagus\u201d is working magic, like a sorcerer does, but it draws directly upon Malfeas. Just use Gifts and Rites? How would I reflect a grimoire, using only W20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T13:14:02-07:00","id":1493760,"title":"","content":"In Rage Across New York, they gave the leaders of the Seventh Generation cult various powers, but they weren't defined as fomori. I would use them as a template. They had Rage and Gnosis. They had whatever Gifts they needed to simulate any inherent powers. The Gifts were different for each individual, and they didn't appear limited in any way. Whatever power the writer wanted them to have, they had that as a Gift regardless of whether it was breed, auspice, tribal, etc. This was before the Book of the Wyrm, so they didn't even have Wyrm Gifts. The text never stated explicitly how they had these powers, but it can be inferred it was a result of a special Rite they used, &quot;the Rite of the Pentarch&quot;. You can use similar explanation for any Rage, Gnosis, or Gifts you want them to have.<br /> <br /> If you want them to have &quot;spells&quot; and &quot;grimoires&quot; then you create Rites for them to use. Just have the Rites be cast from reading the grimoires, or learning from grimoires prior to performing them. You'll just need to create a lot of Rites to do whatever you want them to do. I frequently adapt Call of Cthulhu scenarios to Werewolf, and I just swap the spells of CoC as &quot;Rites&quot; in Werewolf. These &quot;Rites&quot; would be similar to Garou Rites, but would not work for them as they are done according to different principles than Garou Rites which are powered by the Pact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T13:16:17-07:00","id":1493763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1493730-wyrm-cults#post1493730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How to simulate human Wyrm cults without using other splats? I\u2019d like a cult led by a \u2018magus\u2019, but he\u2019s not a mage, Sorcerer, shapeshifter or Kinfolk. How to do this? Maybe give him some special \u2018mark\u2019, visible or invisible, that allows him to learn Rank One Wyrm Gifts and Rank One Wyrm Rites? Make him a particularly clever fomor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Give them whatever you like. They don't need to follow the same rules as PC's anyway, so choose what you feel they need. Gifts are useful shorthands for quick powers and anything they do as longterm rituals can either be set dressing or have magical effects of your choosing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T13:18:41-07:00","id":1493765,"title":"","content":"Ok, cool! Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T17:31:24-07:00","id":1493788,"title":"","content":"Would Vhujunka be appropriate for a cult that thinks its worshipping aliens?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T22:36:45-07:00","id":1493804,"title":"","content":"In my own chronicles I map Vhujunka to the &quot;Serpent Men&quot; of Robert Howard, Clark Ashton Smith, and Lovecraft, But there is no reason why they couldn't be interpreted as aliens. They certainly seem other worldly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T02:54:30-07:00","id":1493810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1493730-wyrm-cults#post1493730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How to simulate human Wyrm cults without using other splats? I\u2019d like a cult led by a \u2018magus\u2019, but he\u2019s not a mage, Sorcerer, shapeshifter or Kinfolk. How to do this? Maybe give him some special \u2018mark\u2019, visible or invisible, that allows him to learn Rank One Wyrm Gifts and Rank One Wyrm Rites? Make him a particularly clever fomor?</div> </div> </div> </div>I use a homebrew half-splat that uses Gnosis and Gifts for 'Witchcraft' to make it distinct from sorcery. Basically use a werewolf theurge template and strike Rage, stepping sideways, and shapechanging. It works quite well in the context of witches / witchers, most Gift effects and the closeness to Spirits are thematically well placed in the associated folklore.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T09:07:16-07:00","id":1493829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1493730-wyrm-cults?p=1493810#post1493810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use a homebrew half-splat that uses Gnosis and Gifts for 'Witchcraft' to make it distinct from sorcery. Basically use a werewolf theurge template and strike Rage, stepping sideways, and shapechanging. It works quite well in the context of witches / witchers, most Gift effects and the closeness to Spirits are thematically well placed in the associated folklore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I\u2019ll use this option!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T12:30:10-07:00","id":1493847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1493730-wyrm-cults?p=1493804#post1493804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my own chronicles I map Vhujunka to the &amp;quot;Serpent Men&amp;quot; of Robert Howard, Clark Ashton Smith, and Lovecraft, But there is no reason why they couldn't be interpreted as aliens. They certainly seem other worldly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I agree, Vhujunka are quite terrestrial, albeit eldritch prehuman horrors, but, from the cult\u2019s perspective, these things are \u201cCLEARLY\u201d alien/extraterrestrial. The cult\u2019s witch uses \u2018devices\u2019 (Wyrm Gifts with unnecessary, non-functioning Vhujunka gadgetry) to \u2018cast\u2019 ancient \u2018spells\u2019 from \u2018the old masters amidst the stars\u2019. Basically, they\u2019re the Thal\u2019hune, except in the service of active demonolatry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}